# Implementation Plan - AyuTrace: Agri-Fresh & Spoilage 0% Intelligence Engine

Building **AyuTrace**, an autonomous GIS surplus routing, predictive spoilage diagnostics, and dynamic clearance pricing platform for agricultural cooperatives and cold-chain logistics networks.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The application will be created as a full Next.js 14/15 App Router application with Tailwind CSS, Leaflet/React-Leaflet dark GIS map, Turf.js spatial clustering, OSRM 2-opt TSP routing engine, live IoT decay telemetry simulator, multi-tier dispatch engine, dynamic flash-sale clearance portal, and interactive B2B booking flow.
> Once verified locally, the codebase will be committed to Git and set up for the repository at `https://github.com/priyanshu-sarjan/Bharat-Academix.git`.

---

## Proposed Architecture & Component Design

### 1. Technology Stack
- **Framework:** Next.js (App Router, React 19, TypeScript)
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS, Custom Dark Logistics Theme (`#0B0F17` obsidian canvas)
- **Map Engine:** Leaflet & React-Leaflet with CartoDB Dark Matter tiles, custom SVG markers for surplus hotspots, moving cold-chain truck icons, dynamic heat-rings, and colored TSP polyline routes.
- **Spatial & Algorithmic Engines:**
  - `Turf.js`: Regional cluster radius deduplication (50m cluster radius) and convex hull bounding.
  - `OSRM + 2-Opt TSP Solver`: Multi-stop route optimization with real-time waypoint polyline rendering.
  - `Dynamic Decay Simulator`: Temperature-dependent exponential decay function ($>8^\circ\text{C}$ spike logic).
- **State & Data:** Zustand store for real-time telemetry, active clusters, trucks, flash offers, and audit logs.
- **Icons & UI:** Lucide React, Framer Motion for smooth tab transitions and telemetry badges, Recharts for telemetry trend charts.

